{
  "_comment": [
    "The shipped Lightspeed X-Series scenario. Every id is written by hand in an",
    "obviously sequential pattern so a reader can tell a seeded id from a minted",
    "one; the shapes are the vendor's, the values are not copies of any real",
    "account's. seed/constants.py names each of them and tests/unit/lightspeed/",
    "test_seed.py asserts the two agree.",
    "",
    "Two outlets and one register each: two rows make a list route's page",
    "boundary crossable, and two registers put the documented rate-limit quota at",
    "300 x 2 + 50 = 650 requests per five-minute window.",
    "",
    "Three payment types, one of them internal, because the payment_types:read",
    "scope is documented as 'excluding internal payment types' and a scenario",
    "with no internal type could not show that.",
    "",
    "Six products: three standalone and a family of three (the tee, which holds",
    "no stock itself, plus its two variants, which do), so that ?sku=, ?name=",
    "(which selects a FAMILY) and ?variants=true are all testable without",
    "creating anything first. The bottle is seeded inactive, which is what makes",
    "include_inactive on the inventory-levels report mean something.",
    "",
    "Ten inventory rows -- every stock-holding product at both outlets -- two",
    "custom adjustment reasons (a CUSTOM adjustment can only ever name one of",
    "these; the tag that would create a third is deferred), two adjustments",
    "already in the log so GET /stock_adjustments has a page boundary, one",
    "customer group and three customers.",
    "",
    "Money and quantities are decimal STRINGS here and JSON numbers on the wire:",
    "a scenario file is read by people and diffed by machines, and a float in",
    "JSON is neither exact nor stable. Prices are stated both ways at the same",
    "0.15 rate the vendor config derives with, so nothing here depends on that",
    "derivation.",
    "",
    "No 'version' anywhere: the Lightspeed version is drawn from the retailer's",
    "one monotonically increasing counter at hydrate, in the order below."
  ],
